  "notices": [
   {
    "scope": "selection",
    "text": "Each cube is one detector cell coloured by the energy-weighted mean Shap-CAM of the segmentation network (absolute frame) over the selection's hits in the cell, Σ E·v / Σ E over every hit of both showers that carries a value, on the one-event view's fixed linear ramp [−1, 1]. Cubes are ranked and capped by the cell's mean energy per selected event. Every energy in this body (the cap block, the depth profile, the exact values) is a mean per selected event, in GeV per event."
   },
   {
    "scope": "selection",
    "text": "One exact scan of the projection table, never the preview sample, sums the 1,000 hits of the N = 2 selected events by detector cell (ix, iy, iz): both showers together, A, B and 'A+B' rows alike, as Page 1's absolute-frame projections sum them. N is the number of selected events, the selection count every absolute-frame response reports. The channel's mean is taken over the hits in the cell, weighted by their energy, so an event weighs in proportion to the energy it deposits there."
   },
   {
    "scope": "selection",
    "text": "Cube positions are the laboratory lattice coordinates measured at ingest; the per-shower coordinate columns are not read in this frame."
   },
   {
    "scope": "selection",
    "text": "Per-axis half-widths: each axis's own energy-weighted 0.1st–99.9th percentile range of the selection's cells (both showers, summed over its 2 events), plus one cell footprint across the beam and one layer pitch along depth, so the cells at either end are drawn whole, never below 150 mm and snapped outward to 20 mm (x 1,980 mm, y 1,020 mm, z 560 mm here). The box keeps one scale on all three axes (1:1:1), so each side is as long as its axis's span; cells snap it to whole cells. The cells beyond it are counted with the cap, below."
   },
   {
